CodingButter__cardboard	R242	Do not pad voice chunks to reach the 20-second target; cut content from a chunk that lacks substance instead.
CodingButter__cardboard	R243	When a voice response is genuinely short, use a single chunk and do not artificially split it.
CodingButter__cardboard	R244	For every response, begin the turn with a mcp__voice__synthesize call before anything else.
CodingButter__cardboard	R245	When calling mcp__voice__synthesize, omit the play_local parameter and pipe the returned URL through the response's "Recommended playback" command in a background Bash.
CodingButter__cardboard	R246	Keep the spoken text of each voice synthesis call to one paragraph or less.
CodingButter__cardboard	R247	Make the spoken text a concise summary of what is about to happen or what just finished, not the full detailed response.
CodingButter__cardboard	R248	After the voice call, write the full detailed text response below it.
CodingButter__cardboard	R249	Never use the long detailed response itself as the spoken text in a voice synthesis call.
CodingButter__cardboard	R250	At the start of every turn, make the voice synthesize tool call first and the playback Bash command second, before any other work.
CodingButter__cardboard	R251	Make `mcp__voice__synthesize` the first tool call of each turn, omitting the `play_local` parameter.
CodingButter__cardboard	R252	Run the recommended playback Bash command without `run_in_background` so playback runs in the foreground and blocks until the audio finishes.
CodingButter__cardboard	R253	Make any other tool calls only after the synthesize and playback calls have been made.
CodingButter__cardboard	R254	Do not place any other tool call between the synthesize call and the playback Bash call.
CodingButter__cardboard	R255	Do not batch the synthesize call in parallel with other tool calls.
CodingButter__cardboard	R256	When producing multiple voice responses in one turn, run each as synthesize then foreground playback then next work, in series.
CodingButter__cardboard	R257	If the turn's voice output was missed or only an intro was voiced, pipe the substantive voice immediately even if it is late.
